`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"tiled",children:"Tiled"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A tile-map editor with JavaScript extensions and command-line export. Extensions can manipulate maps and tilesets; the scripting guide includes TypeScript definitions and CLI evaluation since 1.9. UI-dependent APIs may do nothing or return null in CLI mode, so editor scripts need a headless-path check."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://doc.mapeditor.org/en/stable/manual/scripting/",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mapeditor/tiled/blob/master/COPYING",children:"Tiled COPYING"}),". The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/asset-validation-contracts/#tile-map-identity-geometry-and-runtime-delivery",children:"tile-map transfer contract"})," covers map-local IDs, geometry, sparse coordinates and distinct runtime/persistence observations."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"ldtk",children:"LDtk"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A 2D level editor with structured JSON exports for engine integration. The official format provides full and minimal JSON schemas for levels, layers and entities. Importers must track format changes and deprecations; a JSON export does not supply runtime behavior or establish a command-line editor interface."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://ldtk.io/json/",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/deepnight/ldtk",children:"LDtk repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"aseprite",children:"Aseprite"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A pixel-art and animation editor with batch sprite-sheet export. The CLI can export sprite sheets and companion metadata without opening the UI. Option order and layer visibility affect results. Source availability does not mean permissive redistribution: consult the project EULA for binaries and source use."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.aseprite.org/docs/cli/",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite",children:"Aseprite licensing"}),". The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/asset-validation-contracts/#sprite-atlas-metadata-and-playback-delivery",children:"sprite delivery contract"})," adds pinned trimming, atlas, tag, pivot and timing evidence for a proposed restricted importer."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"inkscape",children:"Inkscape"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"An SVG editor with command-line export and object-geometry queries. Useful for vector UI assets and repeatable raster exports. Actions replace the older verbs interface, which was removed in 1.2; examples on the official wiki span versions, so check the target build’s available actions."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://wiki.inkscape.org/wiki/Using_the_Command_Line",children:"Official documentation or repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"krita",children:"Krita"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A raster-art editor with Python access to documents, actions and filters. LibKis supports automation inside Krita for painting and asset preparation. The scripting guide does not establish a general headless Python service. Krita’s GPL software license does not restrict ownership of artwork created with it."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.krita.org/en/user_manual/python_scripting/introduction_to_python_scripting.html",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://krita.org/en/about/license/",children:"Krita license"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"spine",children:"Spine"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A 2D skeletal-animation editor with runtime export and batch processing. Most CLI exports can run headless, but image and video export needs a windowing system and OpenGL. Editor exports must match the runtime version. CLI automation remains subject to Spine’s user licensing, rather than becoming unrestricted server use."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://en.esotericsoftware.com/spine-command-line-interface",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://eu.esotericsoftware.com/forum/d/30243-tos-question-about-using-spine-cli-as-an-export-tool",children:"Vendor clarification of Spine CLI licensing"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://us.esotericsoftware.com/spine-export/",children:"Spine export"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"rive",children:"Rive"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"An interactive vector-animation authoring tool with embeddable runtimes. Useful for animated menus and UI state machines. Official runtimes are MIT-licensed, while production runtime export requires an eligible paid editor plan. New editor features can require a runtime update or re-export; runtime licensing does not grant editor access."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/rive-app/help-center/blob/master/runtimes/overview.md",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://rive.app/blog/rive-s-new-9-mo-plan",children:"Rive paid export plan"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"effekseer",children:"Effekseer"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A particle-effect editor with game runtimes and command-line export. The 18.x documentation describes editable/runtime .efkefc files and material-cache export. Older .efkproj and .efk workflows differ. Runtime integration and dependent texture/material packaging remain necessary; an exported effect is not a complete engine integration."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://effekseer.github.io/Helps/18x/Tool/en/ToolReference/index.html",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/effekseer/Effekseer",children:"Effekseer repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"fluent",children:"Fluent"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A localization system for language-aware messages and runtime formatting. Fluent resources let translators express language-specific grammar rather than forcing every locale into the same string structure. JavaScript, Python and Rust implementations are available. It still needs translated resources and host integration; it is not an automatic translation service."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://projectfluent.org/",children:"Official documentation or repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"icu",children:"ICU"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Unicode and internationalization libraries for locale-sensitive text processing. ICU4C and ICU4J supply internationalization APIs for C/C++ and Java. They support text infrastructure rather than translation authoring. Match library and data versions, and check the locale-data footprint shipped with the game."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://unicode-org.github.io/icu/userguide/icu/",children:"Official documentation or repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"harfbuzz",children:"HarfBuzz"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A text-shaping library that converts Unicode text into positioned glyphs. Useful for scripts whose glyph selection and placement cannot be handled by one-character-to-one-glyph mapping. Shaping is only part of a text stack: layout, font rasterization, fallback and UI integration still need separate systems."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://harfbuzz.github.io/what-is-harfbuzz.html",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://harfbuzz.github.io/what-harfbuzz-doesnt-do.html",children:"What HarfBuzz does not do"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.renpy.org/doc/html/license.html",children:"Ren'Py bundled HarfBuzz license"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"freetype",children:"FreeType"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A font library for accessing font files and generating glyph images. FreeType provides a common font API and rasterization, not high-level text layout. Its FTL/GPL licensing choices apply to the library; font files need their own rights review. Pair it with shaping and layout when building multilingual UI."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://freetype.org/freetype2/docs/index.html",children:"Official documentation or repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"ink",children:"ink"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A branching-narrative language with a C# runtime and command-line compiler. Compiled JSON feeds Story; Continue and choices drive progression, while state.ToJson and LoadJson save interpreter state. Host-game UI and external side effects remain separate. The MIT core and community inkjs port should not be assumed version-compatible."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/inkle/ink",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/inkle/ink/blob/35c63e52f1d36060930dc7ed3cfba38ea224b528/Documentation/RunningYourInk.md",children:"Runtime guide at inspected commit"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"renpy",children:"Ren'Py"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A visual-novel framework with command-line compilation, linting, testing and builds. The CLI also supports translation workflows. Preserve compiled .rpyc files across CI builds where the documentation requires them for save compatibility. Mobile and web targets have separate setup requirements; a successful build is not a story or localization test."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.renpy.org/doc/html/cli.html",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.renpy.org/doc/html/license.html",children:"Ren'Py License"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"dialogue-drafting-preserve-preference-edited-acceptance-and-character-references",children:"Dialogue drafting: preserve preference, edited acceptance and character references"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Treat a writer's preferred draft, their edited accepted line and an automatic style score as separate records. A relative choice can still require substantial rewriting or rejection of both alternatives."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Internal drafting workflow."})," Ubisoft's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://news.ubisoft.com/en-gb/article/7Cm07zbBGy4Xml6WgYi25d/the-convergence-of-ai-and-creativity-introducing-ghostwriter",children:"March 2023 Ghostwriter creator account"})," describes writers supplying a character and interaction/utterance type, then selecting and editing proposed NPC barks. Pairwise choices also provide preference feedback. The account describes supporting adoption by production teams; it establishes neither a shipped title using the tool nor a measured end-to-end productivity gain. Its Ernestine backend is not documented as a public executable service."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Separate research evidence."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://aclanthology.org/2023.nlp4convai-1.11.pdf",children:"NLP4ConvAI 2023 SASS paper"})," proposes holding the trained model fixed while changing a character-specific index of authored lines at inference (§1). Pairwise human comparisons of earlier model versions did not achieve acceptable inter-annotator agreement; subjectivity and lossy character summaries complicated evaluation (",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://aclanthology.org/2023.nlp4convai-1.11.pdf#page=7",children:"§6.3, printed p.135"}),"). No agreement statistic or threshold is reported. Qualitative inspection sometimes found small fluency decreases despite improved perplexity. The authors describe internal integration as future work and state that UBISCENES will not be publicly released (",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://aclanthology.org/2023.nlp4convai-1.11.pdf#page=8",children:"§7, printed p.136"}),"). These findings do not establish that SASS powered the demonstrated Ghostwriter implementation. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/studio/laforge/news/7CCHPeIseXSW1P49L4XZ7l/generating-video-game-scripts-with-style",children:"La Forge explanation"})," also identifies narrator text as a poor fit for word-choice style, where game-specific names could bias output."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed review template."})," Start with a frozen, rights-cleared candidate pool and project-owned character material. Preserve the scene facts, character/interaction brief, reference revision, original candidates, relative preference and edited accepted line. Allow rejection of both candidates. Include wrong-voice but lore-consistent lines, fluent but scene-inconsistent lines and narrator cases. Record disagreement and its reasons rather than forcing every pair into a quality ranking."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Review meaning, voice, scene consistency and delivery constraints separately. Carry the accepted revision into ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/production-work-orders/#6-compile-localization-shape-text-and-inspect-accessible-ui",children:"localization and branch checks"}),". A later productivity comparison should count reading, discarding, rewriting and downstream rework alongside independent final-quality judgments. This template is unrun; public reading access does not establish executable availability or reuse permissions for Ubisoft's scripts, models or outputs."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"build-delivery-and-networking",children:"Build, delivery and networking"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"nakama",children:"Nakama"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A game backend for identity, social features, storage and multiplayer. Client SDKs and server runtimes support backend logic and authoritative multiplayer. Running the server still requires database operations and authorization design. Managed hosting and enterprise features are separate from the open-source server and SDKs."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://heroiclabs.com/docs/nakama/",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://heroiclabs.com/nakama/",children:"Nakama licenses and features"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/heroiclabs/nakama-js",children:"Nakama JS SDK"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"colyseus",children:"Colyseus"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A room-based multiplayer framework with matchmaking and synchronized state. The MIT framework uses delta-encoded state synchronization and configurable transports, including WebSockets. Gameplay validation remains application code. Horizontal scaling introduces infrastructure such as Redis and load balancing; state sync alone is not cheat prevention."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/colyseus/colyseus",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.colyseus.io/server/transport",children:"Colyseus transport"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"agones",children:"Agones"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Kubernetes orchestration for fleets of dedicated game servers. Agones manages server allocation, fleets and autoscaling around containerized game servers. It requires Kubernetes operations and a compatible server lifecycle. It does not implement gameplay networking, matchmaking policy or a complete player backend."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://agones.dev/site/docs/overview/",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/agones-dev/agones",children:"Agones repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"gamenetworkingsockets",children:"GameNetworkingSockets"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"A native networking library for reliable and unreliable encrypted messages. The C/C++ library provides transport primitives, not entity serialization, delta encoding or compression. Applications still need signaling and game protocol design. Steam authentication and Steam Datagram Relay access should not be assumed for every standalone deployment."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/ValveSoftware/GameNetworkingSockets",children:"Official documentation or repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"butler",children:"butler"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"itch.io’s command-line build uploader and binary-patch toolkit. Offline patch tooling can reconstruct builds using staging checkpoints. In-place patching skips verification of untouched files unless separately checked. Preserve the exact baseline when resuming, and distinguish local patch generation from authenticated uploads or publishing."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://itch.io/docs/butler/",children:"Official documentation or repository"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://itch.io/docs/butler/offline.html",children:"Offline patching"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"steampipe--steamworks-build-delivery",children:"SteamPipe / Steamworks build delivery"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Steam’s depot-build, beta-branch and content-update distribution system. The uploading guide covers build scripts, rollback and chunk-based updates. Pack-file layout can increase patch size and client disk work even for small content changes. Uploading and releasing require Steamworks partner permissions; documentation access is not publishing authorization."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/uploading",children:"Official documentation or repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"gnu-gettext",children:"GNU gettext"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Translation-catalog tooling for extraction, validation and compiled message resources. msgfmt can check and compile PO catalogs into MO files. Format checks are not proof of translation coverage or linguistic quality. Preserve locale, plural rules, message identifiers and catalog provenance; untranslated or fuzzy entries need separate acceptance rules."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Primary sources: ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.gnu.org/software/gettext/manual/gettext.html",children:"Official documentation or repository"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"world-assets",children:"World assets"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"infinigen-staged-generation-and-export-acceptance",children:"Infinigen staged generation and export acceptance"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Connect procedural generation to the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/production-work-orders/#1-export-an-authored-asset-import-it-and-audit-dependencies",children:"asset transfer workflow"}),", checking output identity and imported behavior at each stage."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"pin-and-version-boundary",children:"Pin and version boundary"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["All repository links below pin inspected main commit ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/commit/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698",children:"224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698"}),", committed 2026-10-14. This tree contains both legacy ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"infinigen"})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/src/infinigen/__init__.py",children:"1.19.1"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"infinigen2"})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/src/infinigen2/__init__.py",children:"2.0.0a3"}),". The contracts below concern the legacy scene manager and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"infinigen.tools.export"})," retained in this commit, not an assertion that the new V2 pipeline shares them."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/docs/source/Infinigen2.md",children:"V2 guide"})," calls 2.0 a preview, with limited indoor objects/arrangements rather than full old-system asset coverage. Its CLI chains generators and exporters, and its authors recommend fixing an alpha version because interfaces can change. Do not replace legacy commands with the V2 CLI while claiming the same reproduction or export contract."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"inputs-and-reproducibility",children:"Inputs and reproducibility"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Legacy scene generation takes scene seed, ordered scene Gin configs/overrides, and task/input/output paths. Dataset management separately takes pipeline configs/overrides and either explicit scene seeds or a meta-seed for choosing scene seeds. Scene config and scheduler config are distinct inputs. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/docs/source/ConfiguringInfinigen.md",children:"configuration guide"})," explains override order, camera-dependent mesh detail and population, and the coarse → populate → render/ground-truth task split; fine-terrain and render tasks can recur across views/time blocks. Preserve camera/frame/detail settings as generation inputs, not merely presentation settings."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Crucially, the pinned ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/docs/source/HelloWorld.md",children:"Hello World guide"})," still warns that identical commands may yield differently arranged scenes, runtimes, and memory use on many platforms. This is a documentation warning, not a reproduction experiment performed here. A fixed seed is therefore an identity/provenance field, not proof of bitwise or geometric determinism."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The legacy task entry point explicitly asserts Blender ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"4.2.0"}),"; the package also pins ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"bpy==4.2.0"}),". Record code SHA plus installed version, Blender/Python/dependency versions, platform, hardware, complete command, config contents/ordering, overrides, seed(s), and camera trajectory. These are proposed acceptance records, not a claimed built-in manifest. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/src/infinigen/core/execute_tasks.py#L347-L378",children:"Task source"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/pyproject.toml",children:"package declaration"}),"."]}),`
