`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/docs/source/ExportingToExternalFileFormats.md",children:"official legacy exporter guide"})," describes baking procedural materials/geometry before standard Blender export. It supports OBJ/FBX/STL/PLY/USDC options, texture resolution and individual-object export; vertex colors are restricted to FBX/PLY. Full-scene export is documented as supported only for USDC in this workflow. Other formats realize dense instances and can exhaust memory; trees also contain instances. This is an Infinigen workflow support limit, not a universal claim that no other format can represent instances."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The guide limits material baking to albedo, roughness, normal and metallicity. It warns about transparency, loss of other material parameters, FBX UV failures, and untested/unsupported animation export. Finite texture resolution is lossy. Export existence is not visual equivalence."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Proposed acceptance gate: reopen in the destination engine; verify dependency/texture resolution, transforms and scale, geometry/instance counts, UVs/normals, triangle and texture budgets, and representative appearance against Blender references. Explicitly flag lost transparency/emission/other channels and unsupported animation. Separately qualify collision, LODs, navigation and gameplay. Keep source blend/dependencies alongside a manifest of exported files and hashes. These engine tests remain unperformed here."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"rights-boundary",children:"Rights boundary"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The pinned ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/LICENSE",children:"LICENSE"})," establishes BSD-3-Clause conditions for code/source and binary redistribution. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen/blob/224598d4a2ff95b4fc928e72c222598b7122c698/README.md#L231-L264",children:"README acknowledgements"})," also discuss dependencies and some procedural code obtained under CC0. Neither inspected passage is an explicit, separate generated-output ownership/license grant. Do not label all exported assets CC0 or inherit BSD automatically from the code label. Record code licensing separately from generated-output rights, added asset provenance, and any pre-generated dataset terms. No separate generated-output terms were located in the inspected official sources; this is a source-coverage limitation, not a finding that use is prohibited or a legal determination."]}),`
