`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"WFC completion is not its Boolean alone."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mxgmn/WaveFunctionCollapse/blob/de7d22e705e816b62b4d613199d0463820fcaef3/README.md#L6-L21",children:"README"})," defines local pattern similarity; simple-tiled propagation enforces adjacency. In ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mxgmn/WaveFunctionCollapse/blob/de7d22e705e816b62b4d613199d0463820fcaef3/Model.cs#L73-L97",children:"Model.Run"}),", propagation failure returns false, but exhausting a nonnegative iteration limit also returns true, without completing the observed assignment. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mxgmn/WaveFunctionCollapse/blob/de7d22e705e816b62b4d613199d0463820fcaef3/Program.cs#L49-L66",children:"Program"})," consequently can print DONE and save an unfinished result. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/mxgmn/WaveFunctionCollapse/blob/de7d22e705e816b62b4d613199d0463820fcaef3/OverlappingModel.cs#L105-L148",children:"OverlappingModel.Save"})," supports averaged unresolved possibilities. A PNG is therefore not a solved-tile witness. The caller tries at most ten times per screenshot; with an explicit seed, each retry uses the same seedStart+i rather than a new seed. A failed attempt does not prove the constraint system unsatisfiable."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"DeBroglie retains three states."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/Resolution.cs",children:"Resolution"})," separates Decided, Undecided and Contradiction. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/TilePropagator.cs#L671-L704",children:"Output conversion"})," can substitute identical default values for unresolved and contradictory cells; retain status and possibility sets, not just the converted map. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/TilePropagator.cs#L407-L430",children:"Step/Run"})," distinguish one selection, potentially several backtracks, from looping to a terminal state. Neither signature supplies a wall-clock deadline."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Pin the actual search configuration."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/docs/articles/features.md#L117-L124",children:"prose guide"})," describes opting into backtracking. However, this tree's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/TilePropagator.cs#L37-L100",children:"Boolean constructor and policy factory"})," map false to Backjump and create a PatienceBackjumpPolicy. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/Wfc/WavePropagator.cs#L72-L90",children:"core constructor"})," enables backtracking for a non-null policy. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/Wfc/WavePropagator.cs#L395-L468",children:"History trimming and recovery"})," apply a depth cap only when MaxBacktrackDepth>0; default zero disables that cap, not the policy. A fresh ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/TilePropagatorOptions.cs",children:"TilePropagatorOptions"})," has enum-default BacktrackType.None, which supplies no policy. The false→Backjump observation is specific to the Boolean overload, not a universal library default. Bounded history can discard earlier choices, so terminal Contradiction must not automatically become a global-unsatisfiability claim. These are static observations, not reproduced defects."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Connectivity requires authored semantics."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/docs/articles/path_constraints.md#L1-L40",children:"Path constraints"})," use adjacency routes. PathSpec treats adjacent path tiles as traversable; EdgedPathSpec additionally requires matching exits. RelevantTiles/RelevantCells determine what must connect: selecting only start and goal leaves other components unconstrained. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/DeBroglie/Constraints/Path/ConnectedConstraint.cs#L42-L77",children:"ConnectedConstraint"})," reports contradictory required components. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/BorisTheBrave/DeBroglie/blob/27b37fa7a54f7c532b52634622f36eddd2a3c7da/docs/articles/constraints.md",children:"Fixed-tile/count constraints"})," supply further authoring surfaces. None establishes key-before-lock progression, encounter pacing or controller traversal by itself."]}),`
