`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Preserve source/runtime versions, sample/tileset hashes and rights, topology/mask/dimensions, periodicity, rotations, adjacency/exit tables, weights, fixed/banned cells, required-room counts and relevant endpoints. Separate hard constraints from aesthetic preferences. Record RNG implementation/seed per attempt, constructor overload, search policy, depth/step/time/memory limits and termination reason."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Require a complete assignment plus independent constraint validation before accepting a solved witness. Distinguish attempt contradiction, undecided/partial state, budget exhaustion, cancellation and execution error. The latter operational outcomes are proposed wrapper states, not upstream enum values. Retain failed attempts and partial evidence; never report all seeds solved from selected successful images. Reserve an unsatisfiable claim for justified exhaustive search under the declared model and constraints."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Specify a small satisfiable control; mutually incompatible fixed-room/adjacency requirements; a locally legal but disconnected start/goal; matching path tiles with mismatched exits; and finite-limit unresolved output. Repeat an explicit failed seed separately from changing seeds. Assert that no incomplete output passes acceptance."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Add an authored key/lock progression graph and required/optional room purposes, then verify the resulting gameplay state sequence independently of geometric connectivity. Link accepted layout identity to existing collider, fresh-navigation and real-controller traversal gates. Preserve deliberate narrow-door and wrong-floor variants. A connected or visually plausible map remains insufficient evidence of the intended experience."}),`
`]}),`
